## Fonts

Load every family below from Google Fonts with `preconnect`, `display=swap` and **no `&text=` restriction**, so the browser downloads Cyrillic only when it is needed. Use the exact family and weight lists from the appendices' font URLs, and add the two fallback families.

| Family | Used by | Cyrillic |
|---|---|---|
| Newsreader | birds display, content-page headings | none: Source Serif 4 supplies Cyrillic glyphs per character |
| Nunito Sans | birds UI and body, content-page text | yes |
| Fraunces | myths display | none: Source Serif 4 supplies Cyrillic |
| Instrument Sans | myths UI and body | not guaranteed: Inter supplies Cyrillic |
| JetBrains Mono | myths labels | yes |
| **Source Serif 4** (added: roman 400, italic 400, optical size 8..60) | Cyrillic fallback for both serifs | yes |
| **Inter** (added: 400, 500, 600) | Cyrillic fallback for Instrument Sans | yes |

```css
.hero[data-volume="birds"] { --serif:"Newsreader","Source Serif 4","Iowan Old Style",Georgia,serif; --sans:"Nunito Sans","Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif; }
.hero[data-volume="myths"] { --serif:"Fraunces","Source Serif 4","Iowan Old Style",Georgia,serif; --sans:"Instrument Sans","Inter","Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif; --mono:"JetBrains Mono",ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace; }
.site { --serif:"Newsreader","Source Serif 4","Iowan Old Style",Georgia,serif; --sans:"Nunito Sans","Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif; }
```

The fallbacks are per-glyph, so Latin text always uses the intended family and only Cyrillic letters (including Ө ө Ү ү) fall through. `<html lang>` follows the active language (`mn` or `en`).

## Shared shell (added around the two viewer pages)

The viewers keep their own chrome (sidebar, tabs, top row), so there is no global header on them. The shell adds the following, in each skin's own style.

### Brand and volume switch

- The brand text becomes **`M Atlas`** (a real link to `/`), in each skin's brand size (Appendix A: 26px, Appendix B: 27px; 21px on phones).
- Under it, the small line (Appendix B's `small` block) shows the volume switch in both skins: two links, `BIRDS · MYTHS` (MN `ШУВУУД · ДОМОГ`), the current volume underlined with a 1px accent line. Skin styles: birds use Nunito Sans 9.5px, tracking .22em, weight 600, uppercase, muted; myths use JetBrains Mono as Appendix B's `small`.

### Top row (right column) and phone top bar

The row is `[search] [EN | MN] [bell] [account]`.

- **Language toggle:** a boxed two-button control, 28px tall, 1px `--line` border, radius per skin (8px birds, 3px myths), buttons `EN` and `MN` at 11px, weight 600, tracking .08em, padding 0 9px. The active button has `--accent` fill and `--accent-ink` text; the fill slides between the two with `.35s var(--ease)`. `role="group"` labelled with the i18n `nav.language`, each button has `aria-pressed`.
- **Bell:** becomes a link to `/notes` (label: "Field notes" / "Тэмдэглэл"). Same look.
- **Account avatar:** the same 24px ink circle, now the **menu button** (label: "Menu" / "Цэс"). There are no accounts in this phase.
- On phones the bar is: brand (left), then the round search button, the toggle, the bell, the avatar.

### Search

The search field is real. It searches the four specimens in the active language (name, Latin name, family, tags, habitat). While typing, up to four results appear in a small dropdown directly under the field (panel background, 1px `--line` border, skin radius, 13px text; each result shows the name, the Latin name in italic and the volume). Arrow keys move, Enter opens, Escape clears. Opening a result from the other volume navigates there with `?specimen=`; from the same volume it selects the tab. No results: one muted line "No match" / "Олдсонгүй". On phones the round search button expands the field over the top bar.

### Menu sheet

A full-screen sheet in the current page's tokens, opened from the avatar, growing out of it with `clip-path: circle()` from the avatar's centre (about 700ms, `cubic-bezier(.76,0,.18,1)`). Contents: five large links (Birds, Myths, Field notes, About, Contact) in the page's serif at `clamp(40px, 7vw, 84px)`, separated by 1px `--line` rules, the active one in `--accent`; the language toggle; a day/dusk button (sun icon, label "Day" / "Dusk"); the email and `FB / IG`. A boxed Close button (36px) at the top right; Escape closes it; focus moves into the sheet and returns to the avatar. Reduced motion: instant.

### Sidebar actions

Appendix A and B's sidebar items now do something:

- **Home** goes to `/`. **Featured** selects the page's default specimen (it keeps `aria-current="page"`).
- A category that holds a specimen (Kingfishers, Fire birds, Sea monsters) selects that specimen's tab.
- Every other category opens `/collections/:slug` (slugs in "Data"), a short in-style page: the category name, its count, and the line given in "Page copy", with links to the volume's open specimens.
- The featured card's "Learn more" link keeps `href="#detail"` and moves focus to the detail card (on phones it opens the bottom sheet to full height).

### Content-page bar

On content pages (`.site`) there is a 64px bar: brand left (the `birds` serif, 26px), inline links (Birds, Myths, Field notes, About, Contact) from 900px up in Nunito Sans 13.5px, then the language toggle and the avatar (menu). Below 900px the inline links hide and only the toggle and the avatar remain. 1px `--line` border at the bottom.

### Slim footer (temporary)

On content pages: panel background, 1px `--line` top border, padding 18px 28px, flex with wrap and 12px gaps. Left `© M Atlas. All rights reserved.`; centre the three legal links (Privacy notice, Terms & policies, Cookie notice); right `FB / IG` (`href="#"` until real URLs are set in `content/brand.js`). 12px Nunito Sans, muted. The next prompt replaces this with the big footer.

### Content-page type

Background `--bg`, text `--ink`. Headings: the site serif, weight 500, `clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px)`, line-height 1, tracking -.025em. Body: Nunito Sans 15.5px / 1.6, max 62ch. Small labels reuse Appendix A's eyebrow style (9.5px, tracking .22em, uppercase, muted, weight 600). Cards: `--panel`, 1px `--line`, radius 6px, padding 22px. Headings and cards rise in on first view (`translateY(12px)` to 0 with opacity, 600ms, `var(--ease)`, 45ms stagger), as the appendices' `rise` animation does. Reduced motion: none.

## Language switching (EN / MN)

- Default language is **Mongolian**. Remember the choice in `localStorage` (`matlas.lang`, inside try/catch) and honour `?lang=en|mn`. Update `<html lang>` and `document.title` on every switch.
- Switching is instant and **does not reload, change the route, reset the 3D model or move the camera**. `setLocale(strings)` rewrites text nodes, labels, `aria-label`s and the info card **in place** (no leaving or rising animation; those play only on a tab switch).
- All visible text comes from `src/i18n/en.js`, `mn.js`, `pages.en.js`, `pages.mn.js`, which must have exactly the same keys. Add `npm run check:i18n`: it fails when key sets differ, when a Mongolian value contains no Cyrillic letter (except values that are scientific names, `MA-` numbers, `EN`/`MN`, `FB / IG` and e-mail addresses), and when the same file has a value of `""`. Missing keys fall back to English.
- Scientific (Latin) names, specimen numbers and the brand name are never translated.

## Mongolian must never break the layout (most important rule)

Mongolian strings are usually 20 to 40 percent longer than English, use Ө ө Ү ү, and uppercase Cyrillic with wide tracking is much wider than uppercase Latin. For every text element:

- No fixed widths on text. Use `min-width: 0`, `max-width` and `clamp()`. Single-line labels get `white-space: nowrap` and `text-overflow: ellipsis` with a `title`; running text wraps with `overflow-wrap: anywhere` and `hyphens: auto`.
- In Mongolian, multiply the letter-spacing of every tiny uppercase label whose tracking is .12em or more by .6 (`[lang="mn"]`).
- **Tabs** keep their 130px width; the name may wrap to two lines (`text-wrap: balance`) and the Latin name stays on one line. The tab row never pushes the stage out of view.
- **Sidebar list** (196px column): the items keep their sizes; labels are short by design (see "Data"), single line with ellipsis. In Mongolian the featured card's paragraph is clamped to three lines and **hidden at `max-height: 760px`** (the appendices hide it at 620px), so the list is never clipped.
- **Name heading** (`h1`) may wrap to two lines: `text-wrap: balance`, `overflow-wrap: anywhere`, no hyphens, line-height unchanged.
- **Trait rows:** in the birds skin the 88px label column may wrap to two lines (`align-items: start`); in the myths skin the value may wrap and stays right-aligned. Tag pills wrap (`flex-wrap`).
- **Hint, caption, scale, era labels:** the hint is `max-width: 60%` and wraps; era labels stay `nowrap` and are anchored by the existing `.l` rule so they never leave the card.
- The top row (search, toggle, bell, avatar) must fit at 300px column width; the search field shrinks first and its placeholder ellipsizes.
- Verify, in **both languages and both volumes**, at 320, 360, 390, 414, 600, 768, 820, 1024, 1100, 1101, 1280, 1440 and 1920 px wide, and at 1366 × 620, 1366 × 700 and 1440 × 900: no horizontal scroll, no clipped or overlapping text, no label wrapping where it must not, the 3D model never covered by a panel except where the appendices say so, the bottom sheet on phones never taller than 40dvh. Fix the cause in CSS, not by shrinking fonts below the appendices' sizes.

