## Language files

Both files export one nested object with identical keys. Placeholders in braces (`{n}`, `{pct}`, `{family}`, `{no}`, `{name}`, `{count}`) are replaced by a tiny `format(string, values)` helper in `i18n/index.js`. Where the appendices write a string in English, the English value below is that string. Strings that differ between the two volumes sit under `birds` and `myths`.

`document.title` is `{page name} · M Atlas`, where the page name is `nav.birds`, `nav.myths`, `nav.notes`, `nav.about`, `nav.contact`, the note's title, the category label, the legal page title, or `pages.notFound.title`. `<meta name="description">` is `meta.description`.

Dates (field notes, legal pages) are formatted by one helper: English `5 Nov 2026` (`Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short', year: 'numeric' })`), Mongolian `2026.11.05` (year, month and day with two digits, joined by dots).

