## Page copy and page layouts

All content pages use `.site` tokens, the content-page bar, the content-page type and the slim footer from the master layer above. Every page is a React component that reads its words from `pages.en.js` / `pages.mn.js` and renders in the active language, instantly, when the language is switched. Content width: `max-width: 1100px`, side padding `clamp(20px, 4vw, 28px)`, top padding 56px, bottom padding 88px. Section spacing 72px (48px on phones). All of these pages rise in with the content-page `rise` animation.

Shared small pieces:

- **Link button:** padding 12px 20px, radius 6px, `--accent` background, `--accent-ink` text, 14px weight 600; hover raises it 2px (`translateY(-2px)`, .25s `var(--ease)`); focus ring `2px solid var(--accent)` with 3px offset. Secondary variant: transparent, 1px `--line` border, `--ink` text, hover border `--accent`.
- **Volume tag:** 8px dot in `--accent-birds` or `--accent-myths` followed by `nav.birds` / `nav.myths` (for `both`: two dots and `notes.bothVolumes`), 12px muted.
- **Specimen cut-out** (used on the About cards and the collection page): the specimen's `image`, `object-fit: contain`, with its name and Latin name under it.

### `/about`

1. Hero: eyebrow (`about.eyebrow`), h1 (`about.title`), intro paragraph (17px / 1.55, max 62ch, margin-top 18px).
2. **Two volumes** (`about.volumesTitle`, h2 in the site serif, 400, 28px): two cards in a two-column grid from 760px, one column below. Each card: `--panel`, 1px `--line`, radius 6px, padding 26px, **3px top border** in the volume's colour (`--accent-birds` / `--accent-myths`); the volume label (`volume.vol.*`) in the eyebrow style, the title in the site serif 34px, the text, the two specimens' cut-outs side by side (each 62 × 54 px, contain, with the name in 13px under it), and the call to action (link button, secondary variant, arrow icon `i-arrow`) that goes to `/` or `/myths`. Hover: the card rises 3px (.3s `var(--ease)`).
3. **How to read a plate** (`about.howTitle`): the four `about.steps` in a four-column grid from 900px, two columns from 560px, one below, separated by 1px `--line` rules. Each has a big serif italic number (`01` to `04`, 40px, `--accent`), the title (serif 20px) and the text (14.5px, muted).
4. **Questions** (`about.faqTitle`): the five `about.faq` items as `<details>` elements with 1px `--line` rules between them. The `summary` is the question in the site serif 21px with a chevron (`i-chev`) that rotates 90deg when open (.3s); the answer fades and slides in (opacity and `translateY(-4px)`, .3s). Keyboard: native.
5. **Closing card** (`about.cta`): `--accent-tint` background, radius 6px, padding 32px, title in the serif 28px, text, link button to `/contact`.

### `/notes` and `/notes/:slug`

- `/notes`: header (eyebrow `notes.eyebrow`, h1 `notes.title`, intro `notes.intro`), then the notes, newest first. Each row is a link: three columns from 760px (`150px 1fr auto`), stacked below. Left: date and the volume tag. Middle: the title in the site serif 30px / 1.1 and the excerpt (15px, muted, max 56ch). Right: `notes.minutes`. Rows are separated by 1px `--line`; on hover the row's left padding grows by 8px and the title is underlined (offset 4px), .3s `var(--ease)`. After the list, the **newsletter card** (`pages.newsletter`): `--panel`, 1px `--line`, radius 6px, padding 26px, a title, one line of text and an inline form (e-mail input 44px tall and the submit button; stacked below 560px). Success replaces the form with `newsletter.success` (`role="status"`); failure shows `newsletter.error` (`role="alert"`) under the input.
- `/notes/:slug`: back link (`notes.all`, with a left arrow), meta line (date · volume tag · `notes.minutes`), h1 (the note's title), the body paragraphs (17px / 1.7, max 62ch, 1.1em between paragraphs, the first paragraph 19px). If the note has a `specimen`, a card follows with the specimen's cut-out (70px), its name, and a link button `notes.seeSpecimen` to `/` or `/myths` with `?specimen=`. At the end, **Read next**: the next note in the list (the first when this is the last) as a row like the list rows. An unknown slug renders the not-found page.

### `/contact`

- Header: eyebrow, h1, intro. Below, from 900px, two columns (`minmax(0, 340px) minmax(0, 1fr)`, gap 56px); stacked below.
- Left: a definition list: `contact.emailLabel` with `brand.email` (a `mailto:` link), `contact.socialLabel` with `FB / IG` (the placeholder links from `brand.js`) and `contact.replyLabel` with `contact.replyValue`. Labels in the eyebrow style, values in 17px.
- Right: the **form card** (`--panel`, 1px `--line`, radius 6px, padding 28px). Fields in this order: full name, e-mail, phone (optional), topic (`<select>`), specimen (a `<select>` of the four specimens in the active language, shown **only** when the topic is `feedback`, sliding open with `grid-template-rows` 0fr to 1fr, .3s), message (textarea, 6 rows), consent checkbox, submit button. Labels sit above the fields, 12.5px weight 600. Inputs are 44px tall, `--bg` background, 1px `--line` border, radius 6px, 15px text; focus: `--accent` border and a 3px ring of `color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent)`. A honeypot input named `website` is off-screen (`position: absolute; left: -9999px`), `tabindex="-1"`, `autocomplete="off"`, `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Behaviour: validate on submit with the same rules as the server (name 1 to 120 characters, e-mail valid and at most 254, phone at most 40, message 1 to 2000, consent ticked); field errors in 12.5px, colour `#b3261e` (day) or `#f2998f` (dusk), `aria-describedby`, focus moves to the first invalid field. The client creates one `requestId` with `crypto.randomUUID()` when the form mounts and reuses it for retries; a new one is created after a success. While sending, the button is disabled and shows `form.sending`. Success replaces the form with `form.success` (`role="status"`, focus moves to it); a network or server error shows `form.error` (`role="alert"`) above the button and keeps the typed values.

### `/collections/:slug`

Unknown slug: not found. Otherwise: eyebrow `collection.eyebrow`, h1 the category label, the line `collection.line` with `{name}` the label and `{count}` the sub-label (`sidebar.count.{volume}`), a short rule, then `collection.open` and a grid of the volume's specimens (two columns from 560px): each card shows the cut-out (110px), name, Latin name, and a link button `collection.view` to the viewer with `?specimen=`. The page's accent is the volume's colour.

### `/legal/:slug`

Unknown slug: not found. The title, `legal.updatedLabel` plus `legal.updated`, and the numbered sections (`01.` in the eyebrow style, the heading in the site serif 22px, the paragraph, max 62ch). No other chrome.

### Not found (`*`)

A centred block: h1 `notFound.title` in the serif `clamp(44px, 7vw, 88px)`, the text, and two link buttons (`notFound.birds` to `/`, `notFound.myths` to `/myths`, secondary variant).

